# Vendor Verse — environment variables
#
# This template needs NO environment variables to run. `pnpm install && pnpm dev`
# works with this file absent, and nothing in src/ reads a variable at boot.
# Copy this file to `.env` only if you want to set the one optional value below.
#
# Never commit a real `.env` — .gitignore already excludes `.env` and `.env.*`
# while keeping this example file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute origin used for the <loc> entries served by /sitemap.xml.
# The sitemap protocol requires absolute URLs, so search engines will reject the
# generated sitemap while this is unset (paths come out as "/vendors" rather
# than "https://your-domain.com/vendors"). No other part of the app reads it.
# Set it before you build for production; a trailing slash is trimmed for you.
#
# BUILD-TIME, NOT RUNTIME: every VITE_-prefixed variable is inlined into the
# bundle by Vite at build time. Changing it on your host and restarting the
# server has no effect — you must rebuild.
#
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://vendor-verse.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately absent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no API base URL, database URL, auth secret, or third-party key,
# because there is no backend, no database and no real authentication. See the
# "What it is not" section of README.md. When you add a real API, this is the
# file to document its variables in — and see docs/05-connect-a-backend.md for
# the module to put the fetches behind.
